            "text": "- Mortgage closing scams involving fake documents or impersonation.\n- Recruitment scams targeting job seekers with fraudulent employment offers.\n- Gift card scams as an emerging Business Email Compromise (BEC) method.\n- Online dating romance scams leveraging emotional manipulation.\n- Fake law firm scams impersonating legal entities to defraud victims.\n- Call center scams operated from India, targeting victims via phone.\n- **Technical Support Scams**: Fraudulent actors posing as IT support to access victims’ systems.\n- **Unemployment Fraud Scams**: Exploiting pandemic-era vulnerabilities to siphon benefits.\n- **VoIP-Enabled Scams**: Use of virtual phone numbers to spoof caller IDs and evade detection.\n- **Phishing via Social Media**: Targeting users through fake profiles or compromised accounts.",
